From 26303059d1053878a0cb4095cd2a5bf64242091e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "@dev/12" <dev-12@main.hh.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:57:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sdk): a throwing close still lets go of the session
 folder, and restart cases release the old store (#37472)

The file-store fence (9bc824b7) holds one writer per folder per process. close() released that lock only
after save(true) and the scope removal succeeded, so a throwing close leaked it and the next store in the
process was refused as a second writer. Release in a finally; the error still reaches the caller.

Cases that restart a host on the same folder kept the old store open, which the fence refuses. They now
open through test/support/restart-stores.ts, which closes the previous store on that folder first (as a
stopped process would), and read persisted chats without taking a writer. A setter after close is refused
by name (sessions.test.ts), so host-close expects that instead of a silent drop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
